"www.ck12.org Reasoning and Proof Review Match the deﬁnition or description with the correct word. TABLE 2.26: Match the deﬁnition or description with the correct word. Deﬁnition Answer 1. 5 = x and y+4 = x, then 5 = y+4 A. Law of Contrapositive 2. An educated guess B. Inductive Reasoning 3. 6(2a+1) = 12a+12 C. Inverse 4. 2, 4, 8, 16, 32,... D. Transitive Property of Equality 5. AB ∼= CD and CD ∼= AB E. Counterexample 6. ∼p →∼q F. Conjecture 7. Conclusions drawn from facts G. Deductive Reasoning 8. If I study, I will get an “A” on the test. I did not get an A. Therefore, I didn’t study. H. Distributive Property 9. ̸ A and ̸ B are right angles, therefore ̸ A ∼= ̸ B. I. Symmetric Property of Congruence 10. 2 disproves the statement: “All prime numbers are odd.” J. Right Angle Theorem Texas Instruments Resources In the CK-12 Texas Instruments Geometry FlexBook® resource, there are graphing calculator activities designed to supplement the objectives for some of the lessons in this chapter. See http://www.ck12.org/ﬂexr/chapter/9687 ."
