"4.3. Triangle Congruence using SSS and SAS www.ck12.org 16. Given: AB ∼= DC,AC ∼= DB Prove: △ABC ∼= △DCB TABLE 4.8: Statement Reason 1. 1. 2. 2. Reﬂexive PoC 3. △ABC ∼= △DCB 3. 17. Given: B is a midpoint of DC AB⊥DC Prove: △ABD ∼= △ABC TABLE 4.9: Statement Reason 1. B is a midpoint of DC,AB⊥DC 1. 2. 2. Deﬁnition of a midpoint 3. ̸ ABD and ̸ ABC are right angles 3. 4. 4. All right angles are ∼= 5. 5. 6. △ABD ∼= △ABC 6. Write a two-column proof for the given information below. 18. Given: AB is an angle bisector of ̸ DAC AD ∼= AC Prove: △ABD ∼= △ABC 19. Given: B is the midpoint of DC AD ∼= AC Prove: △ABD ∼= △ABC"
