"6.6. Chapter 6 Review www.ck12.org Sometimes, Always, Never Determine if the following statements are sometimes, always or never true. 1. A trapezoid is a kite. 2. A square is a parallelogram. 3. An isosceles trapezoid is a quadrilateral. 4. A rhombus is a square. 5. A parallelogram is a square. 6. A square is a kite. 7. A square is a rectangle. 8. A quadrilateral is a rhombus. Table Summary Determine if each quadrilateral has the given properties. If so, write yes or state how many sides (or angles) are congruent, parallel, or perpendicular. TABLE 6.12: Opposite sides || Diagonals bisect each other Diagonals ⊥ Opposite sides ∼= Opposite an- gles ∼= Consecutive Angles add up to 180◦ Trapezoid Isosceles Trapezoid Kite Parallelogram Rectangle Rhombus Square Find the measure of all the lettered angles below. The bottom angle in the pentagon (at the bottom of the drawing) is 138◦."
